**1. LiveShare Split-View Layout System - COMPLETE ✅**

**PHASE 1: Initial Discovery & Backend Fixes**

**Issue 1**: Split-view layout not syncing from host to member tabs
- **Symptom**: Host selects split-view in LiveShareWizard → Host sees screen+camera side-by-side → Members only see fullscreen screenshare
- **Root Cause Discovery Timeline**:
  - **First Suspicion**: Layout not being broadcast (WebSocket issue)
  - **Backend Logs Analysis**: Backend WAS broadcasting layout correctly
  - **Database Investigation**: Found column mismatch - migration created `liveshare_layout` but GORM auto-converted `LiveShareLayout` field to `live_share_layout`
  - **Error**: `column "live_share_layout" of relation "watch_sessions" does not exist`

**Fix 1: Database Column Name** - `backend/internal/models/watch_session.go` (Line 78)
```go
LiveShareLayout string `gorm:"column:liveshare_layout;type:text" json:"liveshare_layout,omitempty"`
```
- Added explicit `gorm:"column:liveshare_layout"` tag to prevent auto-conversion
- Result: Backend can now persist layout to database ✅

**Fix 2: Enhanced Backend Logging** - `backend/internal/handlers/liveshare/liveshare_handler.go` (Lines 97-103, 218-226)
```go
layout, layoutOk := data["layout"].(string)
log.Printf("🔍 [LiveShare] Layout extraction: layout='%s', ok=%v", layout, layoutOk)
if layout != "" {
    broadcastMsg["data"].(map[string]interface{})["layout"] = layout
    log.Printf("📡 [LiveShare] Layout ADDED to broadcast message: %s", layout)
}
```
- Added emoji-tagged logging for layout extraction, persistence, broadcast
- Confirmed backend was working: `📡 Layout ADDED to broadcast message: split-view`

