   - "Pray for: John's surgery, Mary's job interview, Youth mission trip"
   - Can be updated in real-time during service

5. **Sermon Title Banner**:
   - Top banner: "TODAY'S SERMON: Faith in Action"
   - Series branding: "Summer Series: Living Like Jesus"

6. **Offering/Donation Info**:
   - QR code for digital giving
   - Venmo/CashApp/PayPal handles
   - "Text 'GIVE' to 555-1234"

7. **Service Schedule**:
   - "Next Service: Wednesday 6:00 PM"
   - "Youth Group: Friday 7:30 PM"

**Technical Features:**

**Bible API Integration:**
- Provider: Bible.org API (NET Bible) or ESV API
- Endpoint: `/api/bible/verse?reference=John+3:16&translation=ESV`
- Response: `{ "reference": "John 3:16", "text": "For God so loved...", "translation": "ESV" }`
- Cache: Store popular verses in localStorage (reduce API calls)

**Text-to-Speech:**
- Browser API: Web Speech API (built-in, free)
- Feature: "Read Bible Verse Aloud" button
- Voices: Choose from system voices
- Speed/pitch adjustable

**Hymn Lyrics Database:**
- Source: Public domain hymns (Amazing Grace, How Great Thou Art, etc.)
- Format: JSON with verse/chorus structure
- Upload: Church can upload their own worship song lyrics

**Studio Controls (LiveShareManager.jsx):**

```jsx
// Church Mode Controls
<div className="church-controls">
  {/* Bible Verse Selector */}
  <div className="control-section">
    <h4>📖 Bible Verse</h4>
    <input 
      type="text" 
      placeholder="Enter reference (e.g., John 3:16)" 
      value={bibleReference}
      onChange={e => setBibleReference(e.target.value)}
    />
    <select value={translation} onChange={e => setTranslation(e.target.value)}>
      <option value="ESV">ESV</option>
      <option value="NIV">NIV</option>
      <option value="KJV">KJV</option>
      <option value="NKJV">NKJV</option>
    </select>
    <button onClick={fetchAndDisplayVerse}>Show Verse</button>
    <button onClick={readVerseAloud}>🔊 Read Aloud</button>
  </div>
  
  {/* Hymn Lyrics */}
  <div className="control-section">
    <h4>🎵 Hymn Lyrics</h4>
    <select value={selectedHymn} onChange={e => setSelectedHymn(e.target.value)}>
      <option value="">Select Hymn...</option>
      <option value="amazing_grace">Amazing Grace</option>
      <option value="how_great">How Great Thou Art</option>
      {/* ...more hymns */}
    </select>
    <button onClick={showHymnLyrics}>Display Lyrics</button>
    <button onClick={nextVerse}>Next Verse</button>
  </div>
  
  {/* Prayer Requests */}
  <div className="control-section">
    <h4>🙏 Prayer Requests</h4>
    <textarea 
      placeholder="Enter prayer requests (one per line)"
      value={prayerRequests}
      onChange={e => setPrayerRequests(e.target.value)}
    />
    <button onClick={showPrayerTicker}>Show as Ticker</button>
  </div>
  
  {/* Sermon Title */}
  <div className="control-section">
    <h4>📢 Sermon Title</h4>
    <input 
      type="text"
      placeholder="Today's sermon title"
      value={sermonTitle}
      onChange={e => setSermonTitle(e.target.value)}
    />
    <button onClick={showSermonBanner}>Show Banner</button>
  </div>
  
  {/* Offering Info */}
  <div className="control-section">
    <h4>💰 Offering</h4>
    <input type="text" placeholder="Venmo handle" value={venmo} />
    <input type="text" placeholder="CashApp handle" value={cashapp} />
    <button onClick={generateQRCode}>Generate QR Code</button>
    <button onClick={showOffering}>Display</button>
  </div>
</div>
```

**Network Effect Strategy:**

**Phase 1: Pilot Churches (5 churches)**
- Mega church: 5,000 members → 2,000 app installs
- Mid-size church: 500 members → 200 app installs
- Small church: 100 members → 50 app installs
- Online church: 1,000 viewers → 400 app installs
- Youth ministry: 200 students → 150 app installs
- **Total**: 2,800 installs from 5 churches

**Phase 2: Church Networks**
- Denominational networks (Baptist, Methodist, Pentecostal, etc.)
- Para-church organizations (Youth for Christ, Campus Crusade, etc.)
- Missionary organizations (global reach)
- Christian colleges (captive audience)

**Phase 3: Word-of-Mouth**
- Each user invites 2 friends → 2,800 → 8,400 users
- Sunday announcements → "Download WeWatch for live service"
- Church bulletins → QR code to app
- Social media posts → Viral spread

**Competitive Advantage:**
- **vs. Church Streaming Platforms** (Church Online, Resi): No monthly fee ($50-200/mo)
- **vs. Zoom**: Professional graphics, not just screen share
- **vs. YouTube Live**: Built-in Bible tools, no ads
- **vs. Facebook Live**: Better privacy, no algorithm suppression

