## 🎯 CURRENT MISSION (April 16-30, 2026)
**Goal**: Launch PWA + Play Store App by April 30, 2026
**Strategy**: Solo grind, 14-day sprint, focused execution with parallel QA portfolio building

### Phase Breakdown (Launch Sprint):
1. **QA Finalization** (April 16-17): ✅ COMPLETE - 35/35 critical test cases passed
2. **Code Cleanup** (April 18): Refactor backend/frontend, remove dead code, add comments
3. **PWA Implementation** (April 19-23): Service worker, manifest.json, offline mode, push notifications
4. **Play Store Submission** (April 24-27): PWABuilder or Expo APK generation
5. **Launch** (April 30): PWA live, Play Store in review (may approve May 1-7)

### Mobile App Strategy:
**Android (Play Store - Priority):**

**Option A: PWABuilder TWA** (RECOMMENDED - fastest path to Play Store)
- **What:** Wraps your PWA in a Trusted Web Activity (native Android wrapper)
- **Steps:**
  1. Deploy PWA to production (April 23)
  2. Go to https://www.pwabuilder.com/
  3. Enter: `https://letswatchout.com`
  4. Click "Build" → Select "Android"
  5. Download signed APK/AAB package
  6. Create Google Play Console account ($25 one-time fee)
  7. Upload APK/AAB and submit for review
- **Timeline:** 2-3 hours to submit, 1-3 days for approval
- **Benefits:** 
  - No coding needed
  - Full PWA features (offline, push notifications)
  - Auto-updates when you update PWA
  - Smallest APK size (~5MB)
- **Limitations:**
  - Requires PWA to be live and working
  - All features must work in mobile browser

**Option B: Expo Simplified App** (Alternative if PWA insufficient)
- **What:** React Native build without 3D cinema (too heavy for mobile)
- **Steps:**
  1. Create simplified version with 2D only
  2. `npx expo prebuild`
  3. `eas build --platform android`
  4. Submit to Play Store
- **Timeline:** 1-2 days to build, 1-3 days approval
- **Benefits:** Native performance, access to device APIs
- **Limitations:** More maintenance, larger APK (~30-50MB)

**iOS (App Store - Deferred to May/June):**
- **Requirements:** 
  - Apple Developer account ($99/year - budget needed)
  - Mac computer or MacStadium cloud Mac rental ($40/month)
- **Interim Solution:** PWA installable via Safari (Add to Home Screen)
  - Works on iPhone/iPad without app store
  - Users can pin to home screen
  - Limited push notifications (requires iOS 16.4+)
- **Future Build:** Use Expo when budget allows
  - `eas build --platform ios`
  - Submit via App Store Connect
  - Approval: 1-7 days (stricter review process)

**Recommended Launch Approach (April 30):**
1. ✅ Deploy PWA (works on all devices via browser)
2. ✅ Submit Android via PWABuilder (Play Store presence)
3. ⏳ iOS via Safari install (free, no app store)
4. ⏳ iOS App Store (later when $99 budget available)

